{
 "duration": 52.767347,
 "frames": 1583,
 "phrases": [
  {
   "text": "Why do we say okay?",
   "start": 0.16,
   "end": 1.58
  },
  {
   "text": "Blame a newspaper joke.",
   "start": 2.28,
   "end": 3.46
  },
  {
   "text": "In 1839,",
   "start": 4.04,
   "end": 5.24
  },
  {
   "text": "Boston editors had a strange hobby:",
   "start": 5.5,
   "end": 7.6
  },
  {
   "text": "abbreviating words wrong on purpose.",
   "start": 8.119,
   "end": 10.58
  },
  {
   "text": "Enough said became NS for 'nuff said.",
   "start": 11.18,
   "end": 14.62
  },
  {
   "text": "All right became OW for oll wright.",
   "start": 15.24,
   "end": 18.58
  },
  {
   "text": "Then on March 23rd,",
   "start": 19.2,
   "end": 20.72
  },
  {
   "text": "the Boston Morning Post printed OK for oll korrect,",
   "start": 21.0,
   "end": 25.22
  },
  {
   "text": "a misspelled all correct.",
   "start": 25.74,
   "end": 27.52
  },
  {
   "text": "It was a silly joke.",
   "start": 28.14,
   "end": 29.28
  },
  {
   "text": "It should have died with all the others.",
   "start": 29.6,
   "end": 31.2
  },
  {
   "text": "But one year later,",
   "start": 31.66,
   "end": 32.64
  },
  {
   "text": "President Martin Van Buren ran for re-election.",
   "start": 32.9,
   "end": 35.46
  },
  {
   "text": "His nickname?",
   "start": 35.88,
   "end": 36.48
  },
  {
   "text": "Old Kinderhook.",
   "start": 36.96,
   "end": 37.9
  },
  {
   "text": "Okay.",
   "start": 38.44,
   "end": 38.94
  },
  {
   "text": "His fans formed OK clubs and shouted it at every rally.",
   "start": 39.5,
   "end": 43.28
  },
  {
   "text": "Van Buren lost the election,",
   "start": 43.82,
   "end": 45.28
  },
  {
   "text": "but the word won.",
   "start": 45.76,
   "end": 46.98
  },
  {
   "text": "That's why we say okay.",
   "start": 47.56,
   "end": 48.84
  },
  {
   "text": "It started as a spelling mistake made on purpose.",
   "start": 49.32,
   "end": 52.5
  }
 ]
}